      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Melanoidins are high molecular weight, heterogeneous polyphenolic polymers formed late in the reaction; their structure becomes progressively larger and more intricate as the reaction progresses, which directly dictates the brown color observed in the crust. Initially less complex, they mature into larger, cross-linked structures responsible for the deep pigmentation. While most proteins participate, highly compact or cross-linked protein structures, especially those with fewer accessible free amine groups, can exhibit structural resistance to the reactive intermediates even under alkaline conditions.",
      "source": "target",
